[00:09.28]Ben! Why don’t you have a rest and stop playing for a while? I’ve got homework. Ben!
[00:19.52]What’s up, Sally?
[00:21.21]I’ve got English and Geography homework. And you’re playing the guitar – badly!
[00:27.47]Well, it’s my hobby and I have a good time when I practise. I love it.
[00:32.37]Sure. But right now?
[00:36.34]Well, yes! I’m practising now, then I can do my homework later.
[00:41.54]Well, can you do your homework now, please? The same time as me? And then practise the guitar later?
[00:49.55]Erm … well, yes, why not? But help me with my Maths homework, OK?
[00:56.20]Oh, all right!
[01:03.54]Mum, can I take judo lessons?
[01:07.82]Judo? Really? What for?
[01:11.74]Well … it’s good exercise, and some of my friends are learning judo, too.
[01:17.82]I think it’s a great idea.
[01:19.82]Really? Judo for girls?
[01:23.35]Mum!!
[01:24.47]Yes, a friend of mine at work does judo. She loves it and she says it’s very good for making her strong and keeping her healthy.
[01:32.43]That’s right, Dad. And maybe I can make some new friends, too.
[01:38.38]Oh. Well. OK.
[01:41.82]Thanks, Mum! Thanks, Dad!
[01:44.30]Jade! I think that’s kung fu, not judo!
[01:54.68]Harry! It’s time for dinner.
[01:59.18]Come on, Harry. Dinner’s ready.
[02:02.80]Just a minute, Mum. I’m finishing something.
[02:06.50]Harry, it’s dinnertime. Come and eat, we’re having dinner!
[02:12.26]OK, Mum.
[02:16.02]You’re always on your phone. Playing games.
[02:19.80]No, not games, Mum. Puzzles. I’m doing a crossword.
[02:25.62]A crossword? Oh, I hate crosswords. They’re too difficult.
[02:31.18]I love them. They’re great exercise for my brain.
[02:34.56]Are they? Well, OK. You know, you have to look after your brain, right?
[02:41.11]That’s right. Just like you look after me, Mum.
